					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-2515349#post-3060766</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-2515349/scp-rocks-j#post-3060766</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 03 Jul 2017 02:31:08 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Kakroom</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2198340</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>stored in a sound proof</p> </blockquote> <p>Think it should be one word.</p> <blockquote> <p>Shut up Kevin no one likes you!</p> </blockquote> <p>Missing comma.</p> <p>It's certainly rather cute, and I don't mind the interactions between the various characters and Agnew's a fun foil, but I never even chuckled. I don't think it helps that there's a contrast between 'fun, cute rocks that kinda don't like each other' and the 'vulgar cutsie thing that's actually not very innocent because juxtaposition.' It's decent structure-wise, what with the ratcheting up of the interviews followed up by the punchline, but I'm afraid it just didn't really click with me. It could be the fatigue, or that this just isn't my kind of humor.</p> <p>+0 novoting for the fact that it's competent and I can imagine someone enjoying it, but I simply, didn't.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
